@* What Facebook asks of a stream before it takes one. The producer is where the broadcast is
   started and where the key of that broadcast is written, so the live is started there first and
   the key is copied out of it into this configuration - a key taken from any other broadcast is
   refused, and so is the ingest of one that was never started at all. *@
<span class="caption facebook-live-help" style="display: block;" data-facebook-live-notice>
    @T["facebookGoLiveHelp"]
    <a href="@LiveLinkView.FacebookProducerUrl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@LiveLinkView.FacebookProducerUrl</a>
</span>
<ol class="facebook-live-steps">
    <li>@T["facebookGoLiveStep"]</li>
    <li>@T["facebookStreamingKeyHelp"]</li>
</ol>
<p class="caption facebook-key-lifetime">@T["facebookKeyLifetime"]</p>